  "reason": "The best result so far is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 acc. The image modality was very weak in isolation (resnet50: 0.208), yet adding it to the strong RNA pipeline gave a ~3.5% boost, suggesting the image contribution is real but may be limited by encoder quality. Config_038 is a single-variable change from config_032: swapping resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l while keeping all other settings identical (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, concat fusion). This isolates the effect of image encoder capacity on multimodal performance. It is the highest-uncertainty axis remaining: if ViT-L unlocks substantially more image signal, we could see a meaningful jump beyond 0.688; if not, we confirm the image contribution is encoder-agnostic and can focus remaining budget on fusion. With 2 experiments left, this controlled comparison is the most informative use of the next slot."
}

